# Database connection (Supabase PostgreSQL)
#
# Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → Database → Connection string → URI.
# Use the **pooler** host with port 6543 — serverless functions cannot hold
# direct connections open.
#
# The example below is the template; put the real values in Vercel →
# Settings → Environment Variables (production + preview) and locally in .env.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-1-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&sslmode=require"

# Optional: PostgreSQL schema that holds this app's tables.
# Defaults to `praantodo`, which keeps the app isolated from whatever else lives
# in the shared `public` schema of the Supabase project.
# DB_SCHEMA=praantodo
